For now, concentrate on surviving.  Do that for
long enough and eventually you'll be able to
deal with the situation.  How's your food supply?

It's possible to get lucky with a levelport trap,
but AFAIK there's no way to guarantee this.

If you can acquire a cursed potion of gain
level, you can safely get back past them:
become very fast (even temporarily, via
potion) and work the speed system so they
don't get a move while you're on the level.

If you can get scrolls of genocide, that'll
do the trick nicely.

Another option is to acquire a reliable way to
deal with the minotaur, then use Elbereth to
ward off the lich.  (Spend wand of digging
charges on that, or fire or lightning if you can
get them.  Writing in the dust is too unreliable
for something as serious as an arch-lich.)  A
minotaur is pretty tough for a pre-Sokoban
pre-Mines character, although their low MR
means you can magically tame them fairly
reliably.  Scrolls of taming aren't very common
though (I think you're almost as likely to find
the book), and without Minetown you may
have some difficulty identifying what scrolls
you do find.

Do you have reflection?  That would open
up several meaningful attack-wand options
for dealing with the minotaur at range,
standing on Elbereth on the stairs.  You
would of course have to find a decent
attack wand first.  Wands of striking and
magic missile are probably too weak.

> And this game started even promising with
